=== Valkyrie Spider ===
[[File:Aston Martin Valkyrie Spider SCD 24.jpg|thumb|The Valkyrie Spider on display at the 2024 SCD Secret Meet.]]
In August 2021, Aston Martin announced a Spider variant for the 2023 model year. Production commenced in the second half of 2022 with a stated intent of 85 examples being produced.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Misoyannis |first=Alex |date=2021-08-12 |title=2023 Aston Martin Valkyrie Spider revealed: F1-inspired hypercar loses its roof |url=https://www.drive.com.au/news/2023-aston-martin-valkyrie-spider-revealed-f1-inspired-hypercar-loses-its-roof/ |access-date=2023-08-18 |website=Drive |language=en-AU}}</ref> The Valkyrie Spider has a removable carbon fibre roof and trades the coupé model's gullwing doors for a pair of front-hinged dihedral [[butterfly doors]].

{{clear}}

=== Valkyrie LM ===
[[File:Aston Martin Valkyrie LM 02.jpg|thumb|The Valkyrie LM on display at the 2026 Ultimate Supercar Garage.]]
Aston Martin introduced an unrestricted track-only version of the [[Aston Martin Valkyrie AMR-LMH|Valkyrie AMR-LMH]] in June 2025 called the Valkyrie LM, made to celebrate Aston Martin's return to competing for the outright victory at the [[24 Hours of Le Mans]] endurance race.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-06-09 |title=You could own* this Le Mans-spec Aston Martin Valkyrie LM |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/motorsport/you-could-own-le-mans-spec-aston-martin-valkyrie-lm |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250609003624/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/motorsport/you-could-own-le-mans-spec-aston-martin-valkyrie-lm |archive-date=2025-06-09 |access-date=2025-06-12 |work=Top Gear |language=en}}</ref> The car is nearly identical to its racing counterpart, with a few mechanical changes, including the reconfiguration of the Cosworth V12 powertrain in order to use standard fuels and the removal of the [[ballast]], [[muffler]], and the mandated electronics required in both the [[FIA World Endurance Championship]] and the [[IMSA SportsCar Championship]]. It also comes equipped with a set of [[Pirelli]] P-Zero racing slicks. Production is limited to 10 examples.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Silvestro |first=Brian |date=8 June 2025 |title=Aston Martin Valkyrie LM Gives Customers Their Own Le Mans Car |url=https://www.motor1.com/news/761973/2026-aston-martin-valkyrie-lm/ |access-date=12 June 2025 |website=Motor1.com |language=en}}</ref> Through Aston Martin's 'Unleashed' program, owners of the Valkyrie LM are able to drive the car on different racing circuits worldwide with comprehensive support from Aston Martin engineers.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bharath |first=Khris |date=8 June 2025 |title=Aston Martin Valkyrie LM Unleashed: Track-Only Hypercar Limited to Just 10 Units |url=https://news.dupontregistry.com/aston-martin/2026-aston-martin-valkyrie-lm-le-mans-deubts/ |access-date=12 June 2025 |website=[[DuPont Registry]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

